.TH VECTORCRAFT-CLI 1 "November 2026" "VectorCraft 0.24.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vectorcraft\-cli \- VectorCraft from the command line: converter, command runner and MCP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vectorcraft\-cli
.RB [ \-\-safe\-mode ]
.I subcommand
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B vectorcraft\-cli mcp
.RB [ \-\-connect
.I ADDR
|
.BR \-\-headless ]
.br
.B vectorcraft\-cli run
.RB [ \-\-in
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-cmd
.I ID
.RB [ \-\-params
.IR JSON ]
|
.B \-\-commands
.IR FILE | \- ]
.RB [ \-\-export
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B vectorcraft\-cli convert
.I IN OUT
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B vectorcraft\-cli info
.I FILE
.br
.B vectorcraft\-cli commands
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vectorcraft\-cli
runs VectorCraft's editor commands without a window. It needs no windowing system and no GPU.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B mcp
Run an MCP server on standard input and output, so that an AI agent can drive the editor engine. By default it
connects to a running VectorCraft window (started with
.BR "vectorcraft \-\-control 7979" )
and falls back to a headless session in this process;
.B \-\-headless
asks for the headless session only.
.BR \-\-automation\-read\-root " and " \-\-automation\-write\-root
confine the files that the agent's commands read and write to a folder and imply
.BR \-\-headless .
.TP
.B run
Headless batch: open a file or start a new document, run commands in order and export each
.B \-\-export
file in the format its extension picks. Prints one JSON result per step.
.TP
.B convert
Open
.I IN
(any readable format) and export
.I OUT
in the format its extension picks. Options include
.BR \-\-scale ,
.BR \-\-ppi ,
.BR \-\-artboard ,
.BR \-\-range ,
.BR \-\-outline\-text ,
.B \-\-decimals
and
.BR \-\-preserve\-editing .
.TP
.B info
Print a JSON summary of a file: import warnings, title, colour mode, units, artboards, object counts and fonts.
.TP
.B commands
Print the catalogue of editor commands as JSON.
.TP
.BR bench ", " perf
Measure rendering and the performance budgets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-safe\-mode
Run any subcommand without plug-ins.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the full usage, with the lists of readable and writable formats, and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vectorcraft/
The settings and the user's folders that the editor shares with the CLI, such as its Fonts folder.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vectorcraft (1)
.PP
https://getartcraft.com/apps/vectorcraft
